<details open>
<summary><strong>cURL</strong></summary>

```bash
curl --no-buffer \
  -H "Accept: text/event-stream"{{#if headers}} \
{{#each headers}}  -H "{{key}}: {{value}}"{{#unless @last}} \
{{/unless}}
{{/each}}{{/if}}{{#if lastEventId}} \
  -H "Last-Event-ID: {{lastEventId}}"{{/if}} \
  '{{url}}'
```

`--no-buffer` disables curl's output buffering so frames print as they
arrive instead of only once the connection closes.

</details>

<details>
<summary><strong>JavaScript - Browser EventSource</strong></summary>

```javascript
const source = new EventSource('{{url}}');

source.onopen = () => {
  console.log('Connected');
};

source.onmessage = (event) => {
  console.log('Received:', event.lastEventId, event.data);
};

source.onerror = (error) => {
  console.error('Error:', error);
  // EventSource reconnects automatically (using Last-Event-ID) unless closed.
};

// Listen for a named event (anything other than the default "message"):
// source.addEventListener('eventName', (event) => {
//   console.log('Received eventName:', event.data);
// });

// To stop listening:
// source.close();
```

{{#if headers}}
> The native `EventSource` API does not support custom request headers.
> Use the `eventsource` npm package (Node.js) or a `fetch`-based polyfill
> when headers (auth, …) are required — see the cURL example above for the
> raw header values.
{{/if}}

</details>

<details>
<summary><strong>Python - requests</strong></summary>

```python
import requests

headers = {
    'Accept': 'text/event-stream',
{{#each headers}}    '{{key}}': '{{value}}',
{{/each}}{{#if lastEventId}}    'Last-Event-ID': '{{lastEventId}}',
{{/if}}
}

with requests.get('{{url}}', headers=headers, stream=True) as response:
    event_type = 'message'
    for line in response.iter_lines(decode_unicode=True):
        if line is None or line == '':
            event_type = 'message'
            continue
        if line.startswith('event:'):
            event_type = line[len('event:'):].strip()
        elif line.startswith('data:'):
            print(f'Received {event_type}:', line[len('data:'):].strip())
```

</details>
